 Inc. in September 2020. Bit Digital, Inc. was founded in 2015 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Samir  Tabar | Chief Executive Officer | Age 53 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 104 people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 42%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $236K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Bit Digital, Inc. is a micro-cap financial services business with a $239M market cap on $114M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +52% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -17% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $575M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +17.8% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -29.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.3%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 22% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +17.8% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text"